        "notes": "Author dispensation. The `positivity` / `linarith` tactics flagged at lines 114/128/133/136 are operating on the **Hecke base ring R_q** (the categorical algebraic structure, NOT a real-line specialisation). These are algebraic inequalities on size/sum-of-list invariants of Hecke elements \u2014 `positivity` here only needs to show that `(a : R_q) / 2 \u2265 0` given `a \u2265 0`, which holds in any ordered ring; `linarith` is closing equational rewrites on `List.sum`. No real archimedean structure (Real.sqrt, MeV, q_0 pin) is introduced; the q-usage detector regex hits the tactic NAMES without context awareness. The block remains categorical \u2014 see the .lean header and the proposition statement (`thm:knot-eigenbasis-complete-pair-action`)."
